SUMMARY:Monarch Butterfly Day
DESCRIPTION:Monarch Butterfly Day\nSeptember 19\, 2026\n10:00 a.m. – 3:00 p.m.\nJoin us at The North Carolina Arboretum on Sept 19th for a day dedicated to the Monarch Butterfly! \nEach fall the last of the year’s monarchs pass through Western North Carolina during their winter migration to Mexico\, so what better time to celebrate!? From 10:00 a.m. to 3:00 p.m.\, enjoy vendors with monarch themed activities\, crafts and activities in the Playing Woods\, a StoryWalk\, dance demonstrations\, and several guided pollinator walks Check back soon for more information! \nSponsored by: 
URL:https://ncarboretum.org/event/monarch-butterfly-day-4/
CATEGORIES:Events
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://ncarboretum.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Stock-Monarch-Child-scaled-1.jpg
